                "text": "Analyse the training examples:\n\nIn each example:\n- There is a template pattern containing color 1 (blue) and color 2 (red).\n- There are also isolated red (2) pixels (or red sub-patterns) elsewhere in the grid.\n- Notice the relation between the template's red pixels and the other red pixels:\n  - In Example 1:\n    - Template at top: 4x2 bounding box:\n      [1, 2]\n      [1, 1]\n      [2, 1]\n      [0, 1]\n      Red pixels in template are at (row 0, col 1) and (row 2, col 0) relative to the template's top-left.\n    - At the bottom:\n      Red pixels are at (9, 3) and (11, 2).\n      Notice (9, 3) is at offset (0, 1) relative to (9, 2), and (11, 2) is at offset (2, 0) relative to (9, 2)!\n      So the pattern of red pixels in the template matches the isolated red pixels!\n      And in the output, the entire template shape (with blue 1s and red 2s) is stamped at the location of matching red pixels.\n  - In Example 2:\n    - Template at (12, 3) - (13, 4):\n      [2, 1]\n      [2, 1]\n      Red pixels are: (0, 0), (1, 0).\n    - Other red pairs:\n      (3, 1) and (4, 1): identical relative red shape (two vertical 2s).\n      (2, 7) and (3, 7): identical relative red shape (two vertical 2s).\n      (14, 10) and (15, 10): identical relative red shape (two vertical 2s).\n    - For each occurrence of the red pattern, the blue pixels (1s) from the template are added at the corresponding relative positions.\n  - In Example 3:\n    - Template at (9, 4) - (11, 6):\n      [2, 2, 1]\n      [0, 1, 0]\n      [0, 1, 0]\n      Red pixels in the template are at (0, 0) and (0, 1) relative to template top-left (9, 4).\n    - In the grid, we have pairs of [2, 2]:\n      at (0, 0) - (0, 1)\n      at (2, 5) - (2, 6)\n    - Each [2, 2] is filled in with the blue tail [1] below it according to the template!\n\nSo the rule is:\n1. Identify the template pattern that contains both red (2) and blue (1) pixels.\n2. Extract the relative positions of red (2) pixels in